Let a repository's exit node carry only its sessions' traffic to the Git
server, in Settings -> Repository variables, and say so on the repository's
card and in the new-session form.

Under the exit node's field, an "Only for the Git server" checkbox names the
host of the repository's URL. Saving sends exit_node_git_only to
PUT /v1/repo-env (images/server/omnigent_repo_env_api.py) while the exit node
is on, and nothing otherwise: the server keeps what it has, and drops it with
the exit node. The runner then routes only the Git server's addresses through
the exit node (images/runner/tailscale/exit-node-routes.sh).

The card adds "· Git server only" after the exit node, and RepoEnvBadge's
popover says traffic to the Git server and the clone go through it, and other
internet traffic goes out directly. GET /v1/repo-env and
GET /v1/repo-env/names return exit_node_git_only; an older server leaves it
out, which reads as all traffic.
Base: omnigent v0.18.0 (a8676d23e88d), after 0001-0037.
